      "description": "This course is intended to provide basics of electron microscopy. Topics include: group theory and basics of crystal symmetry; electron diffraction and interpretation of crystal symmetry; wave optics and imaging principle of electron microscopy; high-resolution transmission electron microscopy; analytical electron energy microscopy; and laboratory demonstration of specific topics.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "For students in MPhil-PhD Materials Sci & Erg; For students in MPhil-PhD Physics; For students in MSc Physics",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Postgraduate - Research",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Lecture",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Div of Material Science & Erg",
      "academic_org": "Div of Material Science & Erg",
      "learning_outcomes": "1. To master the principle of electron microscopes;\n2. To know the basic instrumentation of conventional electron microscope, and master the basic sample preparation methods;\n3. To master the basic knowledge of crystalline symmetry and group theory;\n4. To understand the theory of electron diffraction;\n5. To master the methods for the interpretation of crystal symmetry through electron diffraction patterns;\n6. To understand the principle of dark field/bright field imaging;\n7. To understand the theory of high-resolution electron microscopy;\n8. To master data analysis skill of high resolution electron microscopy images;\n9. To understanding energy dispersive x-ray, and master data analysis skills in identifying material composition;\n10. To understand electron energy loss spectroscopy method in identifying material chemical composition and electronic structures;\n11. To understand the state-of-the-art in situ techniques in monitoring dynamics of material structural/ compositional/ property changes;\n12. To analyze, judge and solve realistic problems and cases using combinational approaches (including diffraction pattern, dark field/bright field images, high resolution image, EDX, EELS, etc.);\n13. To develop an analytical mind towards materials characterization;\n14. To master basic experimental skills in using electron microscopy based techniques for practical material analysis projects.",
      "assessment_types": {
        "Examination": "40",
        "Others": "60"
      }
    },
